# pywebview's Linux backends are pure GI bindings: without `gi` the frozen
# app cannot open a WebView at all, so the GUI smoke test silently degrades to
# its headless fallback. Ships only as an sdist, so the CI runner needs
# gobject-introspection/cairo dev headers installed before the hash-pinned
# install step. Not needed on Windows (WebView2) or macOS (Cocoa).
#
# Upper bound is load-bearing, not hygiene: PyGObject 3.52 switched from the
# girepository-1.0 to the girepository-2.0 headers, and ubuntu-22.04 (our CI
# runner) has no libgirepository-2.0-dev package at all, so >=3.52 cannot build
# there. Stay on the 1.0 series until the runner image moves.
